<title>USA: LCRA 550 MW Texas coal unit returns to full power.</title>
<headline>LCRA 550 MW Texas coal unit returns to full power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lower Colorado River Authority (LCRA) said Tuesday its 550 megawatt Fayette coal-fired power unit 1 was operating at full power after a maintenance outage.</p>
<p>The unit, in La Grange, Texas, was brought back on line Friday after being shut the weekend of Oct 6 for scheduled maintenance, an LCRA spokesman said.</p>
<p>Fayette units 1 and 2, both rated at 550 megawatts, are equally owned by LCRA and the city of Austin.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627</p>
